{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Therefore I declare without understanding</b> — And since the power and the wisdom are Yours, who is it that can conceal Your counsel? He would then be without knowledge. The meaning: for without knowledge I was, when I sought to conceal Your counsel in the world." "<b>Therefore I declared</b> — A word went forth from my mouth improperly, and I entered into wonders beyond me and did not know. And the truth is I cannot know, only what You make known to me — and this is the meaning of <b>I will ask You</b>."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:42.396118269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}